Verified mapping of the original PACT report Status value to a payment status
(Unpaid, PartiallyPaid or Paid). Empty until each value has been confirmed against PACT;
any unmapped value is shown as Unknown with the original text retained.

Genesys campaign handling. When , every upload batch first resolves a campaign named exactly like its stage
(): an existing campaign with that name is reused, never duplicated;
otherwise one is created (status off) from this template when  is set.

            The shared front half of every EDSM read:


Collections enabled;

the financial-read grant;

the Customer Directory profile, under the caller's own visibility;

the PACT identity;

the verified mapping (cached, or discovered).

Keeps a verified PACT mapping for a bounded time, so Payment tab loads and retries do not re-run contract discovery. v1/contracts/{mobile} writes inside EDSM (contract §8.3), so each call needs a reason.
What it is not: an authorization cache. Every request still checks the Collections financial-read grant and the Customer Directory's department visibility before the cache is consulted. The cache holds only which company/tenant pairs PACT returned for the tenant.
Revalidation (discovery runs again) when:
the entry is older than CollectionsSource:PactMappingTtlMinutes (default 30, at most 24 h). Ownership is never reused indefinitely;
the customer's persisted identity changes. The key is the TigerCS tenant plus the profile's phone numbers, so a new or changed number misses the cache;
EDSM refuses a cached pair (business-rule or validation rejection) and the entry is invalidated;
PACT could not be reached. Failures are never cached, so the next load has a reason to try again.
"PACT answered: no contracts for this tenant" is cached for PactMappingNegativeTtlMinutes (default 5), so retries on an unmapped customer don't each trigger a write.
In-process and per instance, like EDSM's own cache. A restart or a second instance only means one more discovery.

